  "body": "## What changed\n\nPocket and slot recognition, headless (app layer and MCP; no GUI changes).\n\n- **`camcraft_app::recognize`** (new module: `mod`, `walls`, `shape`, `op`):\n  - `pockets_of(world, model)` reads the model's planar-face topology (`geometry::feature`, the same B-rep `list_features` and the pick tools use).\n  - A level, up-facing face is a **floor** when the facets across its outer ring rise from it and lean into it (a concave edge), and those walls face each other across the floor.\n  - Walled all round, it is a **closed pocket**. With wall-less spans it is an **open pocket**. A straight channel (at least 2 widths long, both long sides walled, each end wholly walled or wholly open, area within 3% of the shape) is a **slot**, with each end open, round or square.\n  - Each result carries:\n    - the outer ring (world XY, counter-clockwise), island count and area;\n    - floor Z, top Z (highest wall point) and depth;\n    - the **tightest inside corner radius** (0 = sharp, `None` where no two walls meet) and the **open spans**;\n    - for a slot: centreline ends, **width**, length and end kinds.\n  - Shoulders, corner steps, top faces and a plate around a boss are not pockets.\n- **`recognize::operation_for`** maps a feature onto `CreateOperation`'s inputs, so creating it is one undoable History step with every field editable:\n  - a pocket (or a slot with a square closed end, which a round cap would leave standing) becomes a **2D Pocket** on a pick of the floor face, with `bottom_z` at the selection bottom and `top_z` at the selection bottom + depth;\n  - a slot with round or open ends becomes a **Slot** along its centreline: width, fixed heights, source stock, open ends running full width out to the floor's edge.\n- **MCP `detect_pockets {model, create?, tool?, name?}`** lists the features, each with the floor's `face:0x…` id (the id `list_features` prints) and the operation kind it would create. With `create` it adds that operation, one undo step.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/35-pocket-slot-recognition.md`.\n\nProvenance: the concave-edge depression rule follows Joshi & Chang (CAD 20(2), 1988). The minimum-area rectangle follows Freeman & Shapira (CACM 18(7), 1975). No vendor material was consulted.\n\n## How tested\n\nQuick gate, debug: `pocket_recognition` 10/10, `mcp_pockets` 3/3, `mcp` 13/13, `mcp_pick` 7/7, `mcp_setup` 18/18, `cli` 2/2, `feature` 3/3. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\nPinning tests, on watertight meshes built in code (`crates/app/tests/pocket_support`):\n- `a_rectangular_pocket_is_closed_with_sharp_corners`\n- `a_pocket_with_corner_radii_reports_its_tightest_corner` (r 4)\n- `a_round_ended_closed_slot_is_a_slot_between_its_cap_centres`\n- `a_through_slot_is_open_at_both_ends`\n- `an_open_slot_with_a_square_end_machines_as_a_pocket`\n- `parts_without_pockets_list_none` (plain block, shoulder, corner step, boss)\n- `degenerate_input_refuses_cleanly` (unknown model; NaN, infinite and zero-area facets; a torn half mesh)\n- `a_recognised_pocket_becomes_an_undoable_pocket_that_cuts_to_its_floor`: generates with no Gouge, reaches the floor, stays inside the ring; undo removes it\n- `an_open_slot_machined_as_a_pocket_cuts_its_floor_without_a_gouge`\n- `a_recognised_slot_becomes_a_slot_cut_along_its_centreline`: checks the path geometry exactly; undo removes it\n- MCP: `detect_pockets_lists_a_rounded_pocket_and_creates_its_pocket` (generate + verify ok; undo/redo), `detect_pockets_creates_a_slot_for_a_through_slot`, `detect_pockets_refuses_bad_arguments_by_name`\n\n## Not exercised / known gaps\n\n- **#510 (filed):** every typed Slot whose cutter rides its round cap is reported as a gouge today, recognised or not. The likely cause is the stadium region's chorded caps measured against `GOUGE_TOL`. Until #510 lands, a recognised slot's Slot op refuses to post. Its test checks the path geometry, not the verifier's verdict.\n- **Not recognised:**\n  - through pockets / windows (no floor face);\n  - non-level floors and tilted setup frames (the read is world +Z);\n  - curved slots, T-slots and undercuts.\n  - Each level of a stepped pocket is its own feature.\n- An open pocket's open side is not written into the area controls' open boundary. The tool's corner radius stays uncut where a wall meets an open edge.\n- **GUI entry point:** #511. Not exercised on real STEP parts or by hand. The release-tier heavy lanes were not run.\n\nChangelog: Pocket and slot recognition - `detect_pockets` (MCP) lists a model's closed/open pockets and slots (depth, corner radius, slot width, open sides) and creates the Pocket or Slot that machines one, one undo step (#35)\n\nFixes #35\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
